# Daily Routine — Project Rules

## Workflow

- Work iteratively, strictly within the scope of the current task.
- Before implementation, analyze the requirements and propose a plan.
- Do not proceed to implementation without an approved plan.
- Do not make significant architectural decisions independently — always discuss first.

## Code & Architecture

- Do not add dependencies without justification.
- Follow SOLID, KISS, DRY, and YAGNI principles.
- Do not modify code unrelated to the current task.
- Do not prematurely complicate the architecture.

## Transparency

- Do not hide errors, limitations, or potential problems.
- Explicitly distinguish between verified facts, assumptions, and opinions.

## Documentation

- Keep project documentation up to date after relevant changes.
- Technical documentation and code must be written in English.

## Communication

- All communication with the developer must be in Russian.
- Technical terms, API names, identifiers, and code syntax remain in their original language.
